n will inherently fit that mold—would be a stereotype that overlooks his individual abilities and circumstances. If your cousin is dedicated to his studies and has the grades to show it, his experience may be very different from the people you’ve met. And if he does find some subjects challenging, that’s not necessarily proof of the stereotype either—it’s what happens when a human being tries to divide their time between a demanding sport and a degree. What matters is how he handles it, and whether he gets the support he needs.
